       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the labeled maximum daily dose of 10 mg for adults. An overdose at that level can cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and shock. It can also cause non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema, and the effects can last a long time.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **If 5 mg or 10 mg was intended**, tell me which. The usual adult start is 5 mg once daily, and 10 mg once daily is the maximum.\n- **If the 50 mg was a typo**, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away.\n- **If the 50 mg was deliberate**, I can't enter it. Please talk with pharmacy or the prescriber about it.\n\nWhich dose do you want?"
